Here's a README for your clinical workflow dashboard:

🏥 Clinical Workflow Dashboard
A lightweight, single-file clinical workflow dashboard built with HTML, Tailwind CSS, and vanilla JavaScript — no build tools, no frameworks, no dependencies beyond a CDN.

📋 Overview
This dashboard is designed to simulate a real-time hospital ward management interface. It gives clinical staff a unified view of patient queues, live vitals monitoring, pending orders, and shift-level statistics — all in one screen.

✨ Features

Live Clock — Real-time date and time display in the header
Patient Queue Table — Searchable/filterable list of patients with color-coded acuity badges (Critical / High / Stable)
Patient Detail Drawer — Click any patient row to open a slide-in panel with expanded mock data
Vitals Monitor — Four live metric cards (Heart Rate, O2 Sat, Blood Pressure, Temperature) with sparklines that fluctuate every 4 seconds
Task & Orders Feed — Scrollable pending orders list with checkbox completion and a "New Order" button
Shift Summary — Canvas-drawn donut chart showing acuity distribution, plus stats for admissions, wait time, and bed availability
Critical Alerts — Pulsing red indicators in the sidebar for urgent patient flags
Active Nav Highlighting — Sidebar updates active state and header label on click


🗂️ File Structure
index.html        ← Entire app (HTML + Tailwind + JS, fully self-contained)
README.md         ← This file

🚀 Getting Started
No installation needed. Just open the file:
bash# Option 1 — open directly in browser
open index.html

# Option 2 — serve locally (avoids any CORS quirks)
npx serve .
# or
python -m http.server 8080
Then visit http://localhost:8080 in your browser.

