🎨 Design System
TokenValueUsage--color-navy#0a0f1eBackground, sidebar--color-teal#0fd4c0Accents, borders, highlights--color-alert-red#f43f5eCritical badges, alert indicatorsBody fontDM SansUI labels, headingsData fontIBM Plex MonoAll numeric values
Acuity badges use rounded-sm (not pills) for a precise clinical aesthetic. Card borders are 1px teal at low opacity. The main area uses a subtle CSS grid-line background texture.

📊 Dashboard Sections
Patient Queue
Displays 6 mock patients in a sortable table. Columns include room number, name, age, condition, acuity level, wait time, assigned physician, and action buttons. A search bar filters by name or condition in real time.
Vitals Monitor
Four metric cards update every 4 seconds with randomized fluctuation to simulate live monitoring. Each card shows the current value, a trend arrow, a status label, and a mini Canvas sparkline of recent history.
Task & Orders Feed
A scrollable list of pending clinical orders. Each item has a priority icon, description, patient name, timestamp, and assigned staff. Clicking the checkbox marks it complete with a strikethrough animation. The "New Order" button appends a dummy order to the list.
Shift Summary
A donut chart rendered via Canvas API shows the breakdown of patients by acuity. Below it, three stat pills display today's admissions, average wait time, and available beds. An upcoming discharges list shows the next three estimated discharge times.

⚠️ Disclaimer

This dashboard uses entirely mock/simulated data and is intended for UI demonstration and prototyping purposes only. It is not connected to any real medical system, EHR, or patient database. It must not be used in any real clinical environment.


🔮 Potential Enhancements

Connect to a real backend or FHIR-compliant API
Add authentication and role-based views (physician vs. nurse vs. admin)
Persist task completions to localStorage or a database
Add WebSocket support for true real-time vitals streaming
Build out remaining nav sections (Rounds, Notes, Discharge)
Make the layout fully responsive for tablet use


